:"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in 4.5\nNot reproducable in 4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-8700 CPU @ 3.20GHz (12 threads) - 31.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI noticed that after I baked the lightmap a second time everything stayed dark.\nThen I first tried it in Godot 4.4.1, where everything worked as expected. Back to Godot 4.5, I tried reloading the scene after the bake and suddenly the previously new baked lightmap appeared\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBaking the lightmap the first time should work as intended. As this scene contains a baked csg mesh, delete this, assign a different material to the emissive object and rebake the csg mesh.\nThen try to rebake the lightmap, In godot 4.5 it will look dark like if it didn't bake, while in 4.4.1 it bakes as it should.\nFinally save the scene, close and open again, the baked lighting will apear now.\n\nI also recored this video\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e849a101-9d75-47cb-9fcd-f1efef3b7a2a\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[lightmap_baking.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22370903/lightmap_baking.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"rubberduck9999","id":82282845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyMjgyODQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82282845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubberduck9999","html_url":"https://github.com/rubberduck9999","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubberduck9999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rubberduc